2:[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Hogar\",\"item\":\"https://dottodotfreeprintables.com/es/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Cute\",\"item\":\"https://dottodotfreeprintables.com/es/cute/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Leoncito Adorable\",\"item\":\"https://dottodotfreeprintables.com/es/cute/cute-lion-dot-to-dot-puzzle/\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"CreativeWork\",\"name\":\"Leoncito Adorable\",\"description\":\"Los cachorros de león maúllan antes de aprender a rugir. Dibuja un joven león a través de 74 puntos con esta hoja de trabajo imprimible gratuita para niños de 5 a 9 años.\",\"educationalUse\":\"Fine motor skills, number sequencing\"}"}}],["$","main",null,{"children":[["$","nav",null,{"className":"breadcrumb","aria-label":"Miga de pan","children":[["$","$Lf",null,{"href":"/es/","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":14,"height":14,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-house","aria-hidden":"true","children":[["$","path","5wwlr5",{"d":"M15 21v-8a1 1 0 0 0-1-1h-4a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v8"}],["$","path","1d0kgt",{"d":"M3 10a2 2 0 0 1 .709-1.528l7-5.999a2 2 0 0 1 2.582 0l7 5.999A2 2 0 0 1 21 10v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"}],"$undefined"]}]," ","Hogar"]}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","children":" › "}],["$","$Lf",null,{"href":"/es/cute/","children":"Cute"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","children":" › "}],["$","span",null,{"aria-current":"page","children":"Leoncito Adorable"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"maxWidth":1180,"margin":"0 auto","padding":"0 24px 20px"},"children":null}],["$","div",null,{"className":"puzzle-page-layout section","style":{"paddingTop":0},"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"puzzle-preview-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"puzzle-preview-card","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/images/cute-lion-puzzle-400.webp","srcSet":"/images/cute-lion-puzzle-400.webp 400w, /images/cute-lion-puzzle-600.webp 600w, /images/cute-lion-puzzle-700.webp 700w, /images/cute-lion-puzzle.webp 540w","sizes":"(max-width: 640px) 92vw, (max-width: 960px) 600px, 540px","alt":"Esponjoso cachorro de leon sonriendo entre 74 puntos unidos, ficha gratuita para pequenos","width":540,"height":420,"loading":"eager","fetchPriority":"high","decoding":"async","className":"$undefined","style":{"width":"100%","height":"auto","display":"block","borderRadius":16}}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"puzzle-side-ad","children":null}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"puzzle-details-col","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"Cute"}],["$","h1",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.8rem)"},"children":"Dibujo de cachorro de león punto a punto — Hoja de trabajo gratuita de 74 puntos"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"color":"var(--muted)","fontSize":"1.05rem","lineHeight":1.65,"margin":"14px 0 20px"},"children":"Une 74 puntos para descubrir un adorable cachorro de león. Este puzle imprimible fácil ayuda a los pequeños a practicar la secuencia numérica, el control del lápiz y la concentración."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"meta-chips","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"chip","children":["Ages:"," ",""]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"chip","children":["Dots:"," 1–",0]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"chip chip--free","children":"100% Free"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"margin":"16px 0"},"children":[["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":8,"fontSize":"0.9rem"},"children":"Difficulty"}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"flex","alignItems":"center","gap":10},"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"difficulty","role":"img","aria-label":"Dificultad 1 de 3","style":{"margin":0},"children":[["$","span","1",{"className":"on"}],["$","span","2",{"className":""}],["$","span","3",{"className":""}]]}],["$","span",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"0.85rem","fontWeight":800,"color":"var(--muted)"},"children":"Easy"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"fun-fact-box","children":[["$","span",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1.3rem"},"aria-hidden":"true","children":"!"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Fun fact:"}]," ","El rugido de un león puede oírse hasta a 8 kilómetros de distancia, pero los cachorros no pueden rugir hasta que cumplen unos dos años. ¡Hasta entonces, maúllan!"]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"margin":"20px 0 16px"},"children":null}],"$L10","$L11",["$","$L12",null,{"title":"Leoncito Adorable Conecta los Puntos Imprimible - PDF Gratis","imageUrl":"/images/cute-lion-puzzle.webp","compact":true}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"0.8rem","color":"var(--muted)","marginTop":10,"lineHeight":1.5},"children":"No sign-up needed. Opens as a PDF. Print on US Letter (8.5 × 11 inch) or A4 paper. Free for home and classroom use."}],["$","$Lf",null,{"href":"/es/cute/","style":{"display":"inline-flex","alignItems":"center","gap":6,"marginTop":18,"fontWeight":800,"color":"#d94f70","textDecoration":"none"},"children":"Cute"}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"id":"dot-guide","className":"section","style":{"paddingTop":0,"maxWidth":800,"margin":"0 auto","padding":"0 24px 48px"},"children":[["$","h2",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2rem)","marginBottom":12},"children":["Leoncito Adorable"," ",""]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"color":"var(--muted)","lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":28},"dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"¡El rey de la selva nunca se había visto tan tierno! Con una gran melena esponjosa, mejillas redondas y una cola con borla, este simpático cachorro de león está esperando saltar a tu página. Con 74 puntos, es un reto muy gratificante que se construye sección por sección. Así que afila un lápiz, respira hondo ¡y démosle a este pequeño rey su corona de pelusa!"}}],[["$","div","1–16",{"style":{"marginBottom":24,"paddingInlineStart":16,"borderInlineStart":"3px solid var(--blue-light, #63b3ed)"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1rem","fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":6},"children":["1–16"," — ","La melena esponjosa"]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":6},"children":"Empieza en el punto 1 y avanza hasta el 16 para dibujar la famosa melena esponjosa del león. La melena está formada por muchas ondas y curvas pequeñas, así que es un calentamiento perfecto para el control del lápiz: ve onda por onda y la pelusa irá tomando forma."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":"💡"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact__body","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__label","children":"Fun fact!"}],["$","br",null,{}],"Solo los leones macho tienen melena, y esta se vuelve más oscura y tupida a medida que el león envejece. Los científicos han descubierto que las leonas prefieren a los leones con la melena más oscura y densa: una gran melena es señal de un león fuerte y sano."]}]]}]]}],["$","div","17–32",{"style":{"marginBottom":24,"paddingInlineStart":16,"borderInlineStart":"3px solid var(--blue-light, #63b3ed)"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1rem","fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":6},"children":["17–32"," — ","La cara y la naricita"]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":6},"children":"Continúa del punto 17 al 32 para dar forma a la cara redonda del león, su nariz de botón y sus mejillas suaves. Es la parte más detallada del puzle, con puntos muy juntos: un gran ejercicio de paciencia y precisión para manos en crecimiento."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":"💡"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact__body","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__label","children":"Fun fact!"}],["$","br",null,{}],"Los leones tienen una lengua áspera cubierta de pequeños ganchos llamados papilas. Es tan rugosa que puede raspar la carne de los huesos, pero también la usan con suavidad para asear a sus cachorros y a los miembros de su manada."]}]]}]]}],["$","div","33–48",{"style":{"marginBottom":24,"paddingInlineStart":16,"borderInlineStart":"3px solid var(--blue-light, #63b3ed)"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1rem","fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":6},"children":["33–48"," — ","El cuerpo"]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":6},"children":"Traza los puntos 33 a 48 para dibujar el cuerpo suave y redondeado del cachorro. Aquí las líneas son más largas y fluidas que en la sección de la cara, así que anima a hacer un trazo seguro por línea: un agradable cambio de ritmo tras tanto detalle."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":"💡"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact__body","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__label","children":"Fun fact!"}],["$","br",null,{}],"Los leones son los únicos grandes felinos que viven en grupos familiares llamados manadas. Una manada puede tener hasta 30 leones, y las leonas suelen cuidar e incluso amamantar a los cachorros de las demás."]}]]}]]}],["$","div","49–62",{"style":{"marginBottom":24,"paddingInlineStart":16,"borderInlineStart":"3px solid var(--blue-light, #63b3ed)"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1rem","fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":6},"children":["49–62"," — ","Las patas y las almohadillas"]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":6},"children":"Une los puntos 49 a 62 para añadir las patas robustas y las grandes zarpas suaves. Las zarpas de león son maravillosamente redondas, así que ve despacio en las curvas: líneas firmes y uniformes las harán parecer capaces de sostener a un futuro rey."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":"💡"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact__body","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__label","children":"Fun fact!"}],["$","br",null,{}],"La zarpa de un león adulto puede ser más grande que un plato llano, con garras retráctiles como las de un gato doméstico. Los cachorros practican sus saltos sobre las colas de sus hermanos mucho antes de cazar de verdad."]}]]}]]}],["$","div","63–74",{"style":{"marginBottom":24,"paddingInlineStart":16,"borderInlineStart":"3px solid var(--blue-light, #63b3ed)"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1rem","fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":6},"children":["63–74"," — ","La cola con borla"]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":6},"children":"Termina uniendo los puntos 63 a 74 para dibujar la larga cola con su borla esponjosa en la punta. Solo quedan doce puntos: un final suave y seguro da vida a todo el león. ¡No olvides añadir los bigotes y una sonrisa feliz al terminar!"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":"💡"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact__body","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__label","children":"Fun fact!"}],["$","br",null,{}],"Los leones son los únicos felinos del mundo con un mechón de pelo en la punta de la cola. Dentro de la borla se esconde una diminuta espuela de hueso... ¡y nadie sabe con certeza para qué sirve!"]}]]}]]}]]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"section","style":{"paddingTop":8},"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"Cute"}],["$","h2",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"cla